---
title: Spicy Beef and Bean Chili
source: direct-input
description: lots of peppers so it's quite spicy, also you can make salsa from it
tags: [chili, beef, spicy]
---

> This batch uses 1.5 lb of ground beef. Beans are optional, use kidney beans or pinto beans. Serranos may replace the habaneros if it's too spicy. Makes salsa as well.

Add @garlic{1%bulb}(diced small) and @onion{1-2}(whole, red or yellow, or mixed; diced) to @oil{} and simmer until it begins to steam.

Add @jalapenos{10}(chopped finely) and @habaneros{10}(and/or serranos chopped finely for a less spicy version), and let it simmer for a bit.

Add @roma tomatoes{10}(chopped finely) and the spices: @cumin{1%tbsp}, @paprika{2%tsp}, about @garlic powder{3%tbsp}, @onion powder{1%tbsp}, @pepper flakes{1%tsp}, @MSG{4-5%tbsp}, about @salt{1%tbsp}, @limes{4}(juiced or diced), and @pepper{} to taste. Let it simmer until most of the excess water has boiled away.

Reserve however much of the salsa you want before adding the meat.

Add @ground beef{1.5%lb} and, if using, @?kidney beans{1%can}(or pinto beans). Add @chilli powder{3%tbsp}. Mix well, breaking up the beef, and simmer for about ~{15%minutes}, until the beef is fully cooked and the chili has reached the desired thickness.

Serve.